  "_comment": [
    "The synthetic world the end-to-end dry run reviews (overseer #50).",
    "",
    "Every timestamp is RELATIVE — '-3h' means three hours before the run.",
    "Absolute dates would have made this a time bomb: the freshness SLAs are",
    "measured against the clock, so a fixture pinned to a date in August would",
    "have read as fresh in August and 'stale by 4000 hours' ever after. Same",
    "trap as the _ts(hours_ago=2) tests in CLAUDE.md, one file bigger.",
    "",
    "The four projects are deliberately in four different states, because the",
    "point of an integration fixture is to exercise the joins: a healthy feed, a",
    "stale one, one that is fresh but reporting bad numbers, and the overseer's",
    "own workflow history."
